-    {
-      "id": "US-913",
-      "title": "SSE stream resilience: Last-Event-ID reconnection and token buffer for webchat",
-      "priority": "high",
-      "description": "The webchat widget uses SSE for streaming AI responses but currently does not implement the `Last-Event-ID` header for automatic reconnection, meaning a dropped connection mid-stream forces the user to re-submit their message. Additionally, incomplete SSE frames (split across network packets) are not buffered, causing JSON parse errors on the client.",
-      "acceptanceCriteria": [
-        "Each SSE event is assigned a monotonically increasing `id:` field so browsers can send `Last-Event-ID` on reconnect",
-        "The server resumes streaming from the last acknowledged event ID on reconnect within the same conversation session (max 60 seconds)",
-        "The client-side SSE parser buffers partial messages (lines not ending with `\\n\\n`) before attempting JSON.parse()",
-        "A dedicated `event: error` frame is sent to the client when the upstream LLM call fails, triggering a user-visible error message without leaving an empty assistant bubble",
-        "Playwright test simulates a connection drop mid-stream and asserts the response is completed without user re-submission"
-      ],
-      "technicalNotes": [
-        "SSE `id:` field enables browser-native reconnection via `Last-Event-ID` request header",
-        "Event format: `id: {n}\\nevent: message\\ndata: {json}\\n\\n`",
-        "Buffer pattern on client: `buffer = lines.pop() || ''` retains incomplete final lines between data chunks",
-        "Benchmarks: streaming interfaces feel ~40% faster than buffered even with identical latency",
-        "Reference: https://dev.to/pockit_tools/the-complete-guide-to-streaming-llm-responses-in-web-applications-from-sse-to-real-time-ui-3534"
-      ],
-      "dependencies": [],
-      "estimatedComplexity": "medium",
-      "passes": false
-    },
-    {
-      "id": "US-914",
-      "title": "RAG grounding: constrain AI responses to verified knowledge base and return 'I don't know' for out-of-scope queries",
-      "priority": "high",
-      "description": "Rainbow AI currently allows the LLM to respond from its general parametric knowledge, which can produce plausible but incorrect answers about hostel policies, pricing, and facilities. Implementing Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) grounding ensures responses are anchored to verified `.rainbow-kb/` content, and the model explicitly declines to answer when the retrieved context does not cover the query.",
-      "acceptanceCriteria": [
-        "For every guest-facing AI response, a retrieval step queries the `.rainbow-kb/` (Pelangi) or `.rainbow-kb-southern/` (Southern) knowledge base and injects the top-3 relevant chunks into the system prompt",
-        "The system prompt instructs the model to answer only from the provided context and to respond with a configurable fallback phrase (e.g., 'I don't have that information Ã¢â‚¬â€� please contact us directly') when context is insufficient",
-        "Responses that cite a room price, policy, or facility detail must be traceable to a specific KB file in the conversation log",
-        "A Vitest semantic test asserts that a query about a non-existent policy returns the fallback phrase and not a fabricated answer",
-        "The retrieval latency overhead (embedding lookup) does not exceed 500ms p95"
-      ],
-      "technicalNotes": [
-        "RAG is the most effective grounding technique per industry consensus; anchors outputs to verified KB rather than parametric memory",
-        "Embedding model should match the existing provider (OpenRouter/NVIDIA); use cosine similarity with a minimum relevance threshold (e.g., 0.7)",
-        "The `.rainbow-kb/` directory structure is already in place Ã¢â‚¬â€� this story adds the retrieval pipeline, not KB content",
-        "Reference: https://sendbird.com/blog/ai-hallucination-detection and https://www.k2view.com/blog/grounding-and-hallucinations-in-ai/"
-      ],
-      "dependencies": [],
-      "estimatedComplexity": "large",
-      "passes": false
-    },
