-      "id": "US-916",
-      "title": "Confidence-score based automatic chatbot-to-human escalation with context bundle",
-      "priority": "high",
-      "description": "Industry best practice requires AI chatbots to automatically escalate to human agents when the model's confidence in its response drops below a configurable threshold, rather than delivering a potentially wrong answer. This complements the existing sentiment-based escalation by adding a model-internal signal, and requires passing a structured context bundle to the receiving agent.",
