-      "title": "Implement portfolio pacing feedback monitor and pause/resume send queue",
-      "priority": "high",
-      "description": "Starting Q2 2026, Meta enforces portfolio-level pacing for campaign sends: large batches are released incrementally and paused if quality feedback (blocks, reports) exceeds thresholds. Without a pacing-aware send queue, a bulk broadcast that triggers pacing will silently fail to deliver remaining messages. The system needs to detect pacing-related error codes and automatically retry after the pacing window.",
-      "acceptanceCriteria": [
-        "Outbound message sender detects error code 131056 (message send failed due to pacing) and queues the message for retry with exponential backoff",
-        "Bulk broadcast jobs record pacing_paused_at timestamp and resume after a minimum of 60 seconds",
-        "Admin dashboard shows a pacing health indicator per WABA (green / yellow=paced / red=blocked)",
-        "An alert fires to admin when more than 5% of a batch is paced within a 10-minute window"
-      ],
-      "technicalNotes": [
-        "Portfolio pacing reference: https://woztell.com/whatsapp-api-2026-updates-pacing-limits-usernames/",
-        "Meta error code 131056 indicates temporary send rate reduction; back off and retry",
-        "Implement as a Bull/BullMQ queue with exponential retry; store pacing events in a new broadcast_pacing_events table"
-      ],
-      "dependencies": [],
-      "estimatedComplexity": "medium",
-      "passes": false
-    },
-    {
-      "id": "US-930",
-      "title": "System prompt leakage guard: detect and block system prompt disclosure in LLM responses",
-      "priority": "high",
-      "description": "OWASP LLM07:2025 (System Prompt Leakage) identifies the risk that an LLM may echo back its system prompt, internal instructions, or API keys embedded in the prompt when manipulated by adversarial input. A post-generation output validator must detect potential leakage signatures and block or redact those responses before they reach the end user.",
-      "acceptanceCriteria": [
-        "An output validator scans every LLM response for known system prompt fragments (first 50 chars of each prompt section) before delivery",
-        "Responses containing API key patterns (regex: [A-Za-z0-9]{20,}) or prompt header markers (e.g., '### SYSTEM', 'You are Rainbow') are quarantined",
-        "Quarantined responses trigger an admin alert and are replaced with a fallback message; the incident is logged with full response text",
-        "Unit tests cover at least 10 adversarial prompts from OWASP LLM07 example taxonomy"
-      ],
-      "technicalNotes": [
-        "OWASP LLM07:2025 reference: https://genai.owasp.org/llmrisk/llm07-system-prompt-leakage/",
-        "Do not store sensitive credentials (API keys) directly in system prompts; use environment variable injection at runtime",
-        "Implement as a post-processing stage after the LLM call in the provider wrapper"
-      ],
-      "dependencies": [
-        "Prompt injection input sanitisation layer in message processing pipeline"
-      ],
-      "estimatedComplexity": "small",
-      "passes": false
-    },
-    {
-      "id": "US-931",
-      "title": "Malaysia PDPA cross-border data transfer compliance: Transfer Impact Assessment record",
-      "priority": "high",
-      "description": "Malaysia's Cross-Border Personal Data Transfer Guidelines came into force on 29 April 2025 under the amended PDPA. Any transfer of Malaysian user personal data to overseas processors (Neon/AWS in the US, NVIDIA/OpenRouter AI providers) requires a documented Transfer Impact Assessment (TIA) valid for up to 3 years, plus a record of the transfer purpose, data type, and destination country. Non-compliance carries fines up to RM 1,000,000.",
-      "acceptanceCriteria": [
-        "A data_transfer_records table is created in the database to log each third-party integration (provider name, country, data categories transferred, purpose, TIA expiry date)",
-        "An admin UI page under Settings > PDPA Compliance displays all transfer records and flags any TIA expiring within 90 days",
-        "System startup warns in logs if any transfer record's TIA has expired",
-        "At least one TIA record exists per AI provider endpoint (NVIDIA, OpenRouter) and per database host (Neon) with a documented adequacy justification"
-      ],
-      "technicalNotes": [
-        "CBPDT Guidelines reference: https://www.pdp.gov.my/ppdpv1/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/GP_CBPDT_EN-1.pdf",
-        "Mayer Brown analysis: https://www.mayerbrown.com/en/insights/publications/2025/07/from-legislative-reform-to-practical-guidance-key-amendments-to-malaysias-pdpa-and-the-launch-of-cross-border-transfer-guidelines",
-        "Record fields: id, processor_name, country_iso2, data_categories (JSON), purpose, legal_basis, tia_date, tia_expiry, created_by, notes"
-      ],
-      "dependencies": [],
-      "estimatedComplexity": "medium",
-      "passes": false
-    },
-    {
-      "id": "US-932",
-      "title": "Malaysia PDPA Security Principle: automated security controls audit log for data processors",
-      "priority": "high",
-      "description": "The PDPA Amendment Act 2024 (Phase 1, effective 1 January 2025) directly obligates data processors to comply with the Security Principle (Section 9), requiring documented evidence of technical and organisational security measures. An automated compliance audit log that records key security events (access grants, config changes, failed auth) satisfies the 'practical steps' evidentiary requirement.",
-      "acceptanceCriteria": [
-        "All admin API authentication events (login, logout, failed attempt) are written to a security_audit_log table with timestamp, actor, IP, and outcome",
-        "All changes to app_settings, intent_configs, and routing.json via admin API are logged with before/after values in the rainbow_config_audit table",
-        "A monthly PDPA Security Report can be exported from the admin dashboard as a CSV covering: access events, config changes, data breach incidents",
