-    {
-      "id": "US-933",
-      "title": "WhatsApp Flows: in-chat F&B order form with item selection and quantity picker",
-      "priority": "high",
-      "description": "WhatsApp Flows support multi-screen form experiences with quantity selectors, checkboxes, and dropdowns natively inside the chat. Building an order form as a WhatsApp Flow provides a significantly better UX than conversational back-and-forth ordering, reduces miscommunication, and delivers structured JSON order data via the flow completion webhook for direct POS submission.",
-      "acceptanceCriteria": [
-        "A WhatsApp Flow definition is created covering: screen 1 - menu category selection; screen 2 - item selection with quantity picker; screen 3 - special instructions text input; screen 4 - order summary with confirm button",
-        "On flow completion, the flow_response webhook is processed and parsed into the same order object structure used by the conversational order flow",
-        "The flow is triggerable from the main menu reply button 'Order Food' in WhatsApp",
-        "Flow endpoint (data exchange mode) responds within 3 seconds to avoid WhatsApp timeout",
-        "The flow gracefully handles abandonment (no completion webhook) by sending a follow-up message after 10 minutes"
-      ],
-      "technicalNotes": [
-        "Meta Cloud API interactive flow messages: https://developers.facebook.com/docs/whatsapp/cloud-api/messages/interactive-flow-messages/",
-        "WhatsApp Flows complete guide: https://sanoflow.io/en/collection/whatsapp-business-api/whatsapp-flows-complete-guide/",
-        "This story covers F&B ordering via Flows; the existing 'WhatsApp Flows: in-chat check-in form for hostel guests' story covers the hostel use case"
-      ],
-      "dependencies": [],
-      "estimatedComplexity": "large",
-      "passes": false
-    },
-    {
-      "id": "US-934",
-      "title": "LLM output insecure handling guard: sanitise Markdown and HTML before webchat render",
-      "priority": "high",
-      "description": "OWASP LLM05:2025 (Improper Output Handling) warns that LLM responses rendered without sanitisation can cause XSS or Markdown injection in downstream consumers. The existing bug fix for raw JSON display addresses JSON-format leakage, but does not cover adversarially generated Markdown or HTML tags that could execute JavaScript in the webchat widget's innerHTML renderer.",
-      "acceptanceCriteria": [
-        "All LLM response text passed to the webchat frontend is HTML-entity encoded or sanitised through DOMPurify before insertion into the DOM",
-        "Markdown rendering in the webchat widget uses a safe parser (e.g., marked.js with sanitize:true or rehype-sanitize) that strips script/iframe/object tags",
-        "A test case injects '<script>alert(1)</script>' as an LLM response and asserts it is not executed in the browser",
-        "No innerHTML assignments exist in the webchat widget that receive unsanitised LLM text"
-      ],
-      "technicalNotes": [
-        "OWASP LLM05:2025 Improper Output Handling: https://genai.owasp.org/llmrisk/llm02-insecure-output-handling/",
-        "Use DOMPurify (npm: dompurify) for client-side sanitisation; apply on the WebSocket/SSE message handler",
-        "Server-side: strip or escape HTML entities before sending via SSE stream using he or entities npm packages"
-      ],
-      "dependencies": [],
-      "estimatedComplexity": "small",
-      "passes": false
-    },
