-      "id": "US-938",
-      "title": "Implement OpenTelemetry GenAI semantic conventions for LLM span tracing",
-      "priority": "medium",
-      "description": "The OpenTelemetry GenAI Semantic Conventions (stabilised in 2025) define a standard schema for LLM spans covering prompt tokens, completion tokens, model name, provider, latency, and tool calls. Instrumenting the Rainbow AI LLM provider calls with these conventions allows cost, latency, and quality metrics to be exported to any OTel-compatible backend (Grafana, Datadog) without vendor lock-in.",
-      "acceptanceCriteria": [
-        "Every LLM call emits an OTel span with attributes: gen_ai.system, gen_ai.request.model, gen_ai.usage.prompt_tokens, gen_ai.usage.completion_tokens, gen_ai.response.finish_reasons",
-        "Spans are exported via OTLP to a configurable endpoint (default: stdout in development, OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT in production)",
-        "A Grafana dashboard JSON is included in the repo showing: p50/p95 LLM latency, token throughput, and error rate per provider",
-        "Provider failover events (primary to fallback) are recorded as span events within the parent conversation span"
-      ],
-      "technicalNotes": [
-        "OpenTelemetry AI agent observability blog: https://opentelemetry.io/blog/2025/ai-agent-observability/",
-        "OTel GenAI semantic conventions spec: https://opentelemetry.io/blog/2024/llm-observability/",
-        "Use @opentelemetry/sdk-node + openllmetry-js (Traceloop) for Node.js instrumentation"
-      ],
