-      "id": "US-940",
-      "title": "RAG knowledge base tamper detection: SHA-256 manifest for .rainbow-kb files",
-      "priority": "medium",
-      "description": "OWASP LLM04:2025 (Data and Model Poisoning) and LLM08:2025 (Vector and Embedding Weaknesses) identify that RAG knowledge base documents can be tampered with to introduce adversarial content that biases AI responses. The Rainbow AI knowledge base files loaded and embedded at startup need a tamper-detection layer using file hashes to prevent poisoned entries from reaching the retrieval pipeline.",
-      "acceptanceCriteria": [
-        "At startup, SHA-256 hashes of all .md files in .rainbow-kb/ and .rainbow-kb-southern/ are computed and compared against a stored manifest (kb_manifest.json) committed to the repository",
-        "Any file whose hash differs from the manifest is excluded from embedding and logged as a security event",
-        "An admin endpoint GET /admin/kb/integrity returns a JSON report of all checked files with pass/fail status",
-        "The manifest can be updated via an admin command npm run kb:sign that recomputes hashes after an authorised knowledge base update"
-      ],
-      "technicalNotes": [
-        "OWASP LLM04:2025 Data and Model Poisoning: https://genai.owasp.org/llmrisk/llm04-model-denial-of-service/",
-        "OWASP LLM08:2025 Vector and Embedding Weaknesses: https://www.invicti.com/blog/web-security/owasp-top-10-risks-llm-security-2025",
-        "Use Node.js crypto.createHash('sha256') on file content; store manifest as kb_manifest.json in repo root",
-        "This is distinct from the existing RAG grounding and hallucination detection stories; this story addresses data integrity at load time"
-      ],
-      "dependencies": [],
-      "estimatedComplexity": "medium",
-      "passes": false
-    },
